/** 🆕🆕 D446 — the ATTACKER's bodies in play NARROWED BY A PRINTED ATTACK NAME:
    *"This attack does N damage for each of your Pokémon in play that has the Round
    attack."* — 3 sentences / 6 legal printings, the largest single group in this
    family's residue.

    🛑 **THE NOUN IS A LITERAL HERE AND NOT A CAPTURE, AND THAT IS WHAT REMOVES THE
    NEED FOR AN `allOf`.** The printed phrase is ONE noun ("your Pokémon … that has
    the Round attack"), and this union has no INTERSECTION combinator — deliberately
    (see `anyOf`). Capturing the head noun as well would have produced two filters
    the vocabulary cannot conjoin; spelling "Pokémon" into the pattern makes the
    whole phrase resolve to the single `attackNamePokemon` member that IS it.
    ⚠️ The consequence, stated: this anchor reads the bare "Pokémon" head ONLY.
    *"…for each of your Basic Pokémon in play that has the Round attack."* is not a
    sentence the column prints (measured over all 640 rows) and does not match.

    ⚠️ **THE ATTACK NAME IS `([^.]+)` — A CAPTURE, WHERE THE BODY NOUNS ARE A MAP —
    AND THE DIFFERENCE IS WHICH COLUMN ANSWERS IT.** See `CardFilter.attackNamePokemon`
    for the full argument: a printed attack name is `attacks_json[].name`, a persisted
    column, so a captured name is answerable by construction; D440's refused
    `^(.+) card$` capture was refused because *"Ancient"* is in no column at all.
    The class cannot cross a `.`, so it cannot span a sentence break.

    ⚠️ **IT SITS AFTER THE UNNARROWED PAIR IN BOTH READERS AND THE ORDER IS FREE**:
    `IN_PLAY_BODY_MULTIPLY` requires ` in play.` at END OF STRING and this sentence
    ends `that has the Round attack.`, so neither pattern can match the other's text.
    Measured, not argued — all three rows answer `null` to the D439 anchors at HEAD.

    ⚠️ **NO ADDITIVE TWIN**, for `IN_PLAY_FOE_BODY_MULTIPLY`'s reason: all three
    printed rows are the bare `×` fold and the column prints the "more" form of this
    noun ZERO times. */
const IN_PLAY_ATTACK_NAME_MULTIPLY =
  /^This attack does (\d+) damage for each of your Pokémon in play that has the ([^.]+) attack\.$/;
                                                                                   
                                                                                    
                                                                                   
                                                                        
                                                                       

                                                                                      
                                                                                     
                                                                                     
                                                                                      
                                                                                        
                                                                                       
                                                                                 
                                                                                       
                                                                                 
                                                                 

                                                                                  
                                                                                        
                                                                                        
                                                                                    
                                                                           
                                                                                        
                                                                                        
                      

                                                                                   
                                                                                     
                                                                                      
                                                                                      
                                                                                       
                                                                            
                                                                               
                                                                                   
                                                                                       
                                                          

                                                                                
                                                                                        
                                                                                        
                                                                                      
                                                                                       
                                                                                         
                                                                                   
                                                                                     
                                                                                     
                                                                                      
                                                              
                                                                                       
                                                                                       
                            

                                                                                
                                                                                       
                                                                                      
                                                                                         
                                                                                        
                                                                  

                                                                                 
                                                                                        
                                                                                       
                                                                                      
                                                                                      

                                                                                        
                                                                                       
                                                                                       
                                                                                     
                                                                                      
                                                                  

                                                              
                                                                                         
                                                                                  
                                                                                   
                     
const IN_PLAY_BOTH_SIDES_NAME_MULTIPLY =
  /^This attack does (\d+) damage for each Pokémon in play that has "([^"]+)" or "([^"]+)" in its name \(both yours and your opponent['’]s    $/;
/** The three printed nouns with no parameter, mapped to the `CardFilter` members
    that already spell them. A MAP and not a regex alternation, for
    `CLAUSE_ENERGY_TOKENS`' reason: the accepted vocabulary is a single list rather
    than something somebody edits by hand in two places. */
const IN_PLAY_BODY_NOUNS: ReadonlyMap<string, CardFilter> = new Map<string, CardFilter>([
  ["Pokémon", { kind: "anyPokemon" }],
  ["Basic Pokémon", { kind: "basicPokemon" }],
  ["Evolution Pokémon", { kind: "evolutionPokemon" }],
                                                                          
                                                                                  
                                                                                  
                                                                                 
                                                                            
                                                            
    
                                                                              
                                                                            
                                                                                  
                                                                                   
                                                                                  
                                                          
    
                                                                                   
                                                                                    
                                                                                
                                                                                    
                                                                                 
                                                         
  ["Pokémon ex", { kind: "suffixPokemon", suffix: "ex" }],
  [
    "Pokémon ex and Pokémon V",
    {
      kind: "anyOf",
      filters: [
        { kind: "suffixPokemon", suffix: "ex" },
        { kind: "suffixPokemon", suffix: "V" },
      ],
    },
  ],
                                                                               
                                                                                     
                                                                                  
                                                                                   
                                       
    
                                                                                     
                                                                                
                                                                                 
                                                                                  
                                                                                    
                                                                                     
                                                                                   
                                                                              
                                                                                
    
                                                                                    
                                                                                   
                                                                                 
                                                                                  
                                                                                 
                                                                                   
                                                                                     
                                                                                    
                                                                     
  ["Stage 1 Pokémon", { kind: "stagePokemon", stage: "Stage1" }],
  ["Stage 2 Pokémon", { kind: "stagePokemon", stage: "Stage2" }],
                                                                              
                                                                                    
                                                                                
                                                                                    
                                                                                      
                                                                                   
                                                                                      
                                                                                      
                                           
    
                                                                            
                                                                                     
                                                                                  
                                                                                 
                                                                                      
                                                           
    
                                                                    
                                                                                      
                                                                                      
                                                                     
  ["Charjabug", { kind: "byName", name: "Charjabug" }],
]);
                                                                                
                                                                                   
                                                                               

                                                                                    
                                                                                     
                                                                                    
                                                                             
                                                                                 
                                                                                    
                                 

                                                                                    
                                                                                 
                                                                    
                                                                                     
                                                                                     
                                                                                
                                                                                
                                                                        

                                                                                     
                                                                                       
                                                                                      
                                                                 
const SPREAD_EACH_CLASS_NOUNS: readonly string[] = ["Pokémon ex and Pokémon V", "Pokémon ex"];
                                                                                     
                                                                                     
                                                                                      
                                                                             

                                                                                  
                                                                                   
                                                                                  
                                                                                       
                                                                                  

                                                                                     
                                                                                      
                                                                                      
                                                                                    
                                                                               
                                                                                      
                                                      

                                                                                    
                                                                                 
                                                                                   
                                                                                  
                                                                                      
                                                                                
                                                                                      
                                                                                     
                                                                            

                                                                                     
                                                                                     
                                                                                    
                                                                                  
                                                                                        
                                                                                       
                                                                                      
                                                                        

                                                                                  
                                                           
                                                                                      
                                                                                       
                                                         
const SPREAD_EACH_CLASSED_OPPONENT_POKEMON = new RegExp(
  `^This attack does (  d+) damage to each of your opponent['’]s (${SPREAD_EACH_CLASS_NOUNS.join(
    "|",
  )})  . This attack['’]s damage isn['’]t affected by Weakness or Resistance  .$`,
);
                                                                                 
                                                                                 
                                                                               
                                                                                  
                                                                                
                     
const IN_PLAY_OWNER_NOUN = /^(.+)['’]s Pokémon$/;
/** The TYPED noun ("{G} Pokémon", and the spelled-out "Grass Pokémon" the older
    prints carry). Resolved through `CLAUSE_POKEMON_TYPES` — the map that is TOTAL
    over `POKEMON_TYPES` in BOTH notations and already pinned against it — rather
    than through a fresh table, so a type meaning Grass in one clause of this file
    means Grass in every other one. */
const IN_PLAY_TYPED_NOUN = /^(.+) Pokémon$/;
/** 🆕🆕 D439 — the printed noun between "for each of your " and " in play.",
    resolved to the `CardFilter` that already answers it, or `null` when this file
    has no way to spell it (Ancient) — which keeps the sentence on the loud
    ATTACK_EFFECT_SKIPPED path.

    🆕🆕 **D466 — IT RESOLVES A BENCH NOUN NOW TOO, AND THE NAME IS DELIBERATELY NOT
    CHANGED.** `YOUR_BENCH_FILTERED_SCALE` captures the noun in *"…for each ⟨noun⟩ on
    your Bench."* and hands it here: *"which bodies does this printed noun name"* is
    ONE question and gets ONE answer (D159, and `IN_PLAY_BODY_NOUNS`' own Pokémon-ex
    note), so the ZONE is the anchor's business and the NOUN is this function's. The
    name stays `inPlayBodyFilter` because a RENAME is not free — `D439-vocabulary-
    order-loses-the-owner` is a declared `equivalent` survivor quoting this function's
    body, and D359's discriminator is *"a WIDENING is free and a RENAME is not"*.
    ⚠️ **AND "Stage 1" IS NO LONGER AN EXAMPLE OF THE `null` PATH** — it is a map row
    as of D466. The paragraph below still names it as one and is corrected there.

    🛑 **THE ORDER IS LEGIBILITY AND NOT BEHAVIOUR, AND THAT PARAGRAPH IS HERE
    BECAUSE THE FIRST DRAFT OF IT SAID THE OPPOSITE.** This block originally
    asserted *"order is behaviour here, unlike every regex chain in this file"* —
    reasoning that `IN_PLAY_TYPED_NOUN` (`^(.+) Pokémon$`) also matches
    "Team Rocket's Pokémon" and would swallow it. It does match it, and it does NOT
    swallow it: the typed arm returns only when `CLAUSE_POKEMON_TYPES` RESOLVES the
    token, so an unresolved one falls THROUGH to the next lookup rather than
    short-circuiting to null. **The claim was false the day it was written, and the
    thing that caught it was `D439-vocabulary-order-loses-the-owner` SURVIVING** —
    a mutant written to prove the paragraph, which instead disproved it. It is kept
    as a declared `equivalent` survivor rather than deleted, so the day the sets
    below stop being disjoint it reports `STALE-SURVIVOR` (D427).

    ⚠️ **WHAT IS ACTUALLY TRUE IS THAT THE THREE BRANCHES ARE PAIRWISE DISJOINT,
    AND IT IS MEASURED EXHAUSTIVELY RATHER THAN ARGUED.** The whole vocabulary is
    30 nouns — the 8 exact keys, the 11 `POKEMON_TYPES` names and the 11 `{X}`
    codes — and NOT ONE of them matches `IN_PLAY_OWNER_NOUN`, because no Pokémon
    type name ends in a possessive and no exact key carries an apostrophe.
    🆕🆕 **D467 — THIS ARITHMETIC WAS `25 nouns — the 3 exact keys` UNTIL NOW, AND IT
    HAD BEEN WRONG SINCE D446** (which added two keys and did not update it) and
    wronger since D466 (which added two more). ⚠️ **D466 CORRECTED THE COPY OF THIS
    SENTENCE THAT LIVES IN `D439-vocabulary-order-loses-the-owner`'s `reason` AND
    LEFT THE ORIGINAL — HERE — UNTOUCHED**, so the mutant row and the doc block it
    was transcribed from disagreed by four keys for a whole slice. A figure that
    lives in two files rots in two places and reddens in neither; the count is now
    derived from `IN_PLAY_BODY_NOUNS.size` in
    `benchNounScaling.test.ts` §5, so the next key to land reddens
    instead of lying. So no
    noun can resolve down two branches, and the order is free. Pinned in
    `bodiesInPlayScaling.test.ts` §2 over the whole of `POKEMON_TYPES`, so the day
    a type name gains a `'s` the disjointness rung goes RED and this paragraph
    stops being true LOUDLY.

    ⚠️ **WHAT DOES THE REFUSING IS THE MAP AND NOT THE REGEX**: `(.+) Pokémon` also
    matches "Ancient Pokémon", which MISSES `CLAUSE_POKEMON_TYPES`, falls past the
    owner pattern too, and reaches the trailing `return null`. That is the vocabulary.
    🆕 **D466 — "Stage 1 Pokémon" USED TO BE THE SECOND EXAMPLE HERE AND IS NOT ONE
    ANY MORE**: it is an EXACT KEY now, so it never reaches the typed branch at all.
    The example is replaced rather than the sentence relaxed, because the claim it
    makes ("the map refuses, not the regex") is still true and still needs a witness
    the pool actually prints. */
function inPlayBodyFilter(noun: string): CardFilter | null {
  const exact = IN_PLAY_BODY_NOUNS.get(noun);
  if (exact !== undefined) return exact;
  const owner = IN_PLAY_OWNER_NOUN.exec(noun);
  if (owner !== null && owner[1] !== undefined) {
    return { kind: "ownerPokemon", owner: owner[1] };
  }
  const typed = IN_PLAY_TYPED_NOUN.exec(noun);
  if (typed !== null) {
    const pokemonType = literalClauseRow(CLAUSE_POKEMON_TYPES, typed[1] ?? "");
    if (pokemonType !== undefined) return { kind: "typedPokemon", pokemonType };
  }
  return null;
}
// 🆕🆕 D440 — DAMAGE SCALED BY A COUNT OF FILTERED CARDS IN A DISCARD PILE, ON
// EITHER SEAT. *"This attack does N [more] damage for each <noun> in your
// [opponent's] discard pile."* — measured over `legalAttackCorpus()` (the committed
// `legal_standard = 1` attack column, 640 sentences / 1,732 printings) by running
// the two patterns below against every row.
//
// 🛑 THE WHOLE FAMILY, PRINTED WHOLE AND ON BOTH AXES (D428/D437: never truncate an
// enumeration by rows or by width). The survey pattern is published so its edges are
// visible (D425): every corpus row matching BOTH `/for each/` AND `/discard pile/` —
// **8 hits, every hit read** — which is deliberately looser than either anchor below
// and is what found the two rows a "for each X in your discard pile." shape cannot:
//
//   ADDITIVE ("more"), YOUR pile — 3 sentences / 6 printings reach the anchor:
//     • "This attack does 20 more damage for each Energy card in your discard pile."             2 → anyEnergy
//     • "This attack does 60 more damage for each Ethan's Adventure card in your discard pile."   2 → byName
//     • "This attack does 10 more damage for each Ancient card in your discard pile."             2 → 🛑 NO FILTER (below)
//   MULTIPLY (`×`, no adjective), the OPPONENT's pile — 2 sentences / 4 printings reach it:
//     • "This attack does 30 damage for each Basic Energy card in your opponent's discard pile."  2 → basicEnergy
//     • "This attack does 30 damage for each Item card in your opponent's discard pile."          2 → item
//   MULTIPLY, YOUR pile — 1 sentence / 2 printings reaches it:
//     • "This attack does 20 damage for each Supporter card that has "Team Rocket" in its name in your discard pile."  2 → 🛑 NO FILTER (below)
//   REACHES NEITHER OF THE TWO ANCHORS ABOVE, and each for its own structural reason:
//     • "This attack does 20 damage for each Pokémon in your discard pile that has the United Wings attack."  1 —
//       the noun is SPLIT AROUND the zone phrase, so the sentence does not END at
//       "discard pile." and NEITHER OF THE TWO `^…$` ANCHORS ABOVE can see it at any
//       vocabulary width. 🆕🆕🆕 **D508 BUILT IT ON A THIRD ANCHOR**
//       (`DISCARD_PILE_ATTACK_NAME_MULTIPLY`, two constants down) and this paragraph is
//       corrected in place rather than deleted, because BOTH of the reasons it once gave
//       have now expired and the order in which they did is the finding. It said the row
//       needed *"a `CardFilter` member reading `attacksOf`, which is D439's refused
//       widening one zone over"*; **D446 built that member** (`attackNamePokemon`) and
//       corrected the sentence in `discardPileScaling.test.ts` without correcting it
//       here. What was left was ONE block — this anchor's `$` — and D508 is a new anchor
//       rather than a relaxation of either of these two, so the sentences they claim are
//       untouched. The count and the filter are BOTH shipped; the cross product cost
//       zero members in either union.
//     • "Put 2 damage counters on 1 of your opponent's Pokémon for each Basic {G} Energy card in your discard pile. Then, shuffle those Energy cards into your deck."  3 —
//       a counter PLACEMENT compound, not a damage fold: its count scales an op's
//       amount rather than the attack's damage, so it belongs to no reader in this
//       family. Listed because the loose pattern found it and a survey that silently
//       drops a hit is the defect this file keeps paying for.
//
// So the TWO ANCHORS ABOVE reach 6 sentences / 12 printings and the VOCABULARY claims
// **4 sentences / 8 printings**; the other two fall through `discardPileFilter` to
// null and stay on the loud ATTACK_EFFECT_SKIPPED path. 🆕🆕🆕 **D508 ADDS A THIRD
// ANCHOR AND A FIFTH CLAIMED SENTENCE** (the United Wings row, 1 printing), which this
// family's totals therefore now read **5 sentences / 9 printings** — but the 6/12 and
// 4/8 figures above are UNCHANGED, because they are about these two patterns and this
// map, and D508 touched neither.
//
// 🛑 THE TWO REFUSALS, EACH WITH ITS OWN REASON — NOT ONE REASON TWICE.
//   • **Ancient card** (2 printings) is DATA-BLOCKED and permanently so, not unbuilt.
//     `types.ts`:146-149 settles it and was re-read at D440 word for word — *"are BOTH
//     answerable, because `stage` and `types` are catalog columns; *"Ancient"* (1, Iron
//     Moth sv06.5-009) is not, because / the Ancient/Future banner is printed on the
//     card FACE and appears in NO / field of the persisted catalog and NONE of tcgdex's
//     own card model (checked / upstream against Roaring Moon ex sv04-124, the canonical
//     Ancient print — it"*. A name-keyed species table is refused there FOREVER because
//     the banner is a per-PRINTING fact. **The fix is an INGEST change; nothing in this
//     file can be the fix.** D439 refused the same banner one zone over for the same
//     reason and this is the second reading of one permanent block, not a second block.
//   ✅ **Supporter card that has "Team Rocket" in its name** (2 printings) was the
//     SECOND refusal here and it is **BUILT at D510**. It was never data-blocked: the
//     survey called it UNBUILT and pinned the falsifier on the population, and that
//     falsifier FIRED — `discardPileScaling.test.ts` §6 went RED against the build and
//     was re-pointed rather than narrowed. The block used to argue that a substring
//     reading *"does exist in this file"* for a `BoardCondition`
//     (`yourBenchHasNameContaining`, D392) *"but the two vocabularies do not share a
//     predicate"*; that is still true — they share an OPERATOR and not a question — and
//     `CardFilter.supporterNameContaining` is now the `CardFilter` half.
//     🛑 **AND ONE CLAUSE OF THE OLD TEXT WAS FALSE WHEN IT WAS WRITTEN**: it read
//     *"no `CardFilter` member does substring matching at any width"*, where
//     `ownerPokemon` has matched a proper PREFIX of `Card.name` since D200. Corrected at
//     the member, at `matchesFilter`'s arm and here — D508's rule, swept across
//     `packages                                                                     
  
                                                                                 
                                                                                     
                                                                                       
                                                                                  
                                                                                  
                                                                                     
                                                                                    
                                                                                      
                                                                                  
                                           
  
                                                                                     
                                                                               
                                                                             
                                                                                        
                                                                                      
                                                                                  
                                                                                        
                                                                                        
                                                                                        
                                                                                    
                                                                                      
                                                                                        
                                                                               
                                                                            
                                                                                            
                                                                                        
                                                                                         
                                                                                      
                                                                              
  
                                                                                    
                                                                                     
                                                                          
                                                                                     
                                                                                       
                                         
  
                                                                                     
                                                                                        
                                                                                        
                                                                                      
                                                                                      
                                                                                    
                                                                        
                                   
                                                                                                 
                                
                                                                                                      
                                                                 
                                                                                   
                                                                                      
                                                                                    

                                                                                   
                                                                                    
                                                                                       
                                                                                   
                                                                         
                                                                     
                                                                                       
                                                                                       
                                                                                         
                                                                                    
                                                                          

                                                                                      
                                                                                       
                                                                                        
                                                                                     
                                                                                       
                                                                                     
                                                               

                                                                                    
                                                                                      
                                                                                       
                                                                                     
                                                                                     
                                                                                        
                                                                                 
                                                                                        
                                                                                   
                                                                                     
                                             

                                                                            
                                                                                
                                                                                      
                                                                                 

                                                                              
                                                                                         
                                                                                        
                                                                                         
                                                                                      
                                                                          
                                                                                        
                                                                                      
                                                                                      
                                                                                       
                                                                    

                                                                                      
                                                                                      
                                                                                         
                                                                                  
                             

                                                                               
                                                                                     
                                                      
                                                                                        
                                                                                     
                                                                                      
const DISCARD_PILE_ATTACK_NAME_MULTIPLY =
  /^This attack does (\d+) damage for each Pokémon in your discard pile that has the ([^.]+) attack\.$/;
                                                                                 
                                                                                    
                                                                  
                                                                                     
                                                                              
                                                                                      
                                      
                                                                                
                                                                          
                                                                                       
                                                                                         
                                                                                   

                                                                                       
                                                                                   
                                                                                       
                                                                                     
                                                                                        
                                                                                      
                                                                                   
                                                                                        
                                                                                 
const DISCARD_PILE_NOUNS: ReadonlyMap<string, CardFilter> = new Map<string, CardFilter>([
                                                                                       
                                                                           
  ["Energy card", { kind: "anyEnergy" }],
                                                                                       
                                                                                
                                                                                       
                                                                    
  ["Basic Energy card", { kind: "basicEnergy" }],
                                                                                        
                                                                                      
                                                       
  ["Item card", { kind: "item" }],
                                                                                      
                                                                                      
                                                                                   
                                                                                      
                                                                                   
  ["Ethan's Adventure card", { kind: "byName", name: "Ethan's Adventure" }],
]);
                                                                               
                                                                                    
                                                                                       

                                                                          
                                                                                        
                                                                                        
                                                                                       
                                                                                      
                                                                                       
                                                                                    
                                                                                       

                                                                          
                                                                                    
                                                                                         
                                                                                        
                                                                                       
                                                                       

                                                                           
                                                                                       
                                                                                     
                                                                           
                                                                                         
                                                                                         
                                                                                        
                 
const PILE_SUPPORTER_NAME_FRAGMENT = /^Supporter card that has "([^"]+)" in its name$/;
/** 🆕🆕 D440 — the printed noun between "for each " and " in your[ opponent's] discard
    pile.", resolved to the `CardFilter` that already answers it, or `null` when this
    file has no way to spell it (Ancient) — which keeps the sentence on the loud
    ATTACK_EFFECT_SKIPPED path.

    🆕🆕🆕 **D510 — IT HAS A SECOND BRANCH NOW, AND THE PARAGRAPH BELOW USED TO SAY
    THERE COULD NEVER BE ONE.** The original text read *"ONE lookup and no fall-through
    patterns, unlike `inPlayBodyFilter` one vocabulary up … There is therefore no branch
    ORDER here to be right or wrong about"*, and named the Team Rocket name substring as
    a permanent `null`. Both halves are corrected here rather than left standing: this
    family now has a PARAMETERISED noun exactly as that one does.

    🛑 **THE LITERAL TABLE RUNS FIRST, WHICH IS `boardConditionForClause`'s STATED
    RULE VERBATIM** (*"Literals win by construction, so adding a template can never
    re-interpret a clause a row already owns"*) — followed, not invented. ⚠️ **AND THE
    ORDER IS UNOBSERVABLE ON TODAY'S VOCABULARY FOR A STRUCTURAL REASON RATHER THAN A
    LUCKY ONE, WHICH D503 SAYS TO CHECK**: the pattern demands the literal bytes
    ` that has "`, and this map is CLOSED at four keys none of which contains them — so
    no string can reach both branches, provable by reading the map rather than by
    running the column. The order is kept anyway, because the map is the thing a
    successor adds a key to. */
function discardPileFilter(noun: string): CardFilter | null {
  const literal = literalClauseRow(DISCARD_PILE_NOUNS, noun);
  if (literal !== undefined) return literal;
  const fragment = PILE_SUPPORTER_NAME_FRAGMENT.exec(noun);
  return fragment === null ? null : { kind: "supporterNameContaining", fragment: fragment[1] ?? "" };
}

// 🆕🆕 D488 — MILL YOUR OWN DECK, THEN SCALE THE DAMAGE BY A **FILTERED** COUNT OF
// WHAT WAS MILLED. *"Discard the top N cards of your deck, and this attack does P
// damage for each <noun>[ that] you discarded in this way."* — **2 sentences / 2 legal
// printings**, measured over `legalAttackCorpus()` (the committed `legal_standard = 1`
// attack column, 640 sentences / 1,732 printings) by running the anchor below against
// every row, and transcribed byte for byte:
//
//   1  "Discard the top 3 cards of your deck, and this attack does 80 damage for each
//       Energy card you discarded in this way."                        (corpus line 126)
//   1  "Discard the top 7 cards of your deck, and this attack does 70 damage for each
//       Misty's Pokémon that you discarded in this way."               (corpus line 129)
//
// 🛑 **THEY ARE ONE MECHANISM AND THE CLAIM IS MEASURED BY AXIS DELETION RATHER THAN
// ASSERTED** (D483's four-row cluster split 2+2 under exactly this test, so it is not a
// formality). Three axes were deleted in turn and both rows were re-run against all 13
// readers of `attackReaderSurface()`:
//
//   * delete the FILTER (`Energy card` / `Misty's Pokémon that` -> `card`): both rows
//     collapse to the SAME string at two counts, and BOTH ARE STILL REFUSED. So the
//     filter is not what blocks either of them.
//   * delete the MILL HEAD (put the shipped Energy-discard head under the same filtered
//     tail): STILL REFUSED. So the filtered count is a blocker on its own.
//   * delete the SCALING (drop the tail): both heads build, and to the SAME op at two
//     counts.
//
// **Two blockers, both rows carry both, neither is the noun.** The filters differ in
// KIND — a card CATEGORY against an OWNER-PREFIXED name — and that difference costs
// nothing, because `CardFilter` already spells both (`anyEnergy`, `ownerPokémon`).
//
// ⚠️ **THE HEAD IS SPELLED WITH A COMMA AND THE FAMILY ONE SCREEN UP SPELLS A PERIOD,
// SO THIS ANCHOR IS STRUCTURALLY DISJOINT FROM `DECK_TOP_MILL` AND FROM
// `ENERGY_DISCARD_SCALED_DAMAGE` WITHOUT A GUARD** (D467's kind of disjointness, and
// the reason no ordering here can rot): `DECK_TOP_MILL` ends `of your deck  $` and this
// one demands `of your deck, and` at that offset, so no string matches both; and
// `ENERGY_DISCARD_SCALED_DAMAGE` demands `from (this|your) Pokémon  ` before its tail,
// which no deck mill prints. `deckTopMill.test.ts` already pins the period form's `$`
// against a second sentence riding the same action, and that rung is untouched.
//
// ⚠️ **NARROW ON THREE PRINTED AXES ON PURPOSE, AND EACH IS A MEASUREMENT.** The mill
// is OWN-DECK only (`whose: "self"`) and PLURAL-COUNTED only, because the column prints
// no opponent-side and no singular spelling of this compound at all; and the fold is the
// MULTIPLY one (`does P damage for each`, no printed *"more"*), which is
// `ENERGY_DISCARD_SCALED_DAMAGE`'s own split reproduced one head over — the additive
// twin of this very shape is corpus FILE LINE 130 (*"Discard the top card of each
                                                                                    
                                                                                  
                                                                                    
                                        
  
                                                                                  
                                                                                    
                                                                                 
                                                                                          
                                                                                          
                                                                                  
                                                                                         
                                                                            
  
                                                                                       
                                                                                        
                                                                                       
                                                                                 
  
                                                                                  
                                                                                   
                                                                                      
                                                                                         
                                                                               
                                                                                        
                                                                                      
const DECK_MILL_FILTERED_SCALED_DAMAGE =
  /^Discard the top (\d+) cards of your deck, and this attack does (\d+) damage for each (.+?) (?:that )?you discarded in this way\.$/;
                                                                                  
                                                                                     
                                                                    
                               

                                                                                       
                                                                                     
                                                                                        
                                                                                      
                                                                                        
                                                                                         
                                                                                    
                                                                                       
                                        

                                                                                  
                                                                                        
                                                                                    
                                                                                        
                                                                                    
                                                                                           
                                         

                                                                                    
                                                                                   
                                                                                 
                                                                                      
                                                                                       
                                                                                    
                                                                      

                                                                            
                                                                                      
                                                                                        
                                                                                   
function milledCardFilter(noun: string): CardFilter | null {
  const zoneNoun = discardPileFilter(noun);
  if (zoneNoun !== null) return zoneNoun;
  const owner = IN_PLAY_OWNER_NOUN.exec(noun);
  if (owner !== null && owner[1] !== undefined) return { kind: "ownerPokemon", owner: owner[1] };
  return null;
}
                                                                               
                                                                                  
                                                                  
                                                                                  
                                           
  
                                                                             
                                                                                   
                                                                         
                                                                                   
  
                                                                              
                                                                                          
                                                                                       
                                                                                     
                                                                               
                                                                                  
                                                                                 
                                                                                    
                                                                                  
           
  
                                                                                   
                                                                                  
                                                                                     
                                                                              
                                                                                  
                                                                                  
                                                                                     
                                                                                 
                                                                                    
                                                                             
                                                                                   
                                                                                
                                                                                   
                                                                                    
                                                                                  
                                                                                
                                                                            
                                                                                
                                                                           
                                                                                
                                                                                  
                                                                                    
               
  
                                                                                 
                                                                                 
                                                                                   
                                                                                 
                                                                                   
                                                                                  
                                                   
  
                                                                                     
                                                                            
                                                                                     
                                                                                   
                                                                     
  
                                                                                   
                                                                            
                                                                                 
                                                                               
                                                                                 
                                                          
                                                                                    
                                                                                   
                                                                                  
                                                                              
                                                                                   
                                                                                    
             
  
                                                                                
                                                                             
                                                                     
                                                                                  
                                                                         
const OPPONENT_HAND_COUNT_MULTIPLY =
  /^This attack does (\d+) damage for each ([^.]+) in your opponent['’]s hand  $/;
const ATTACK_REVEAL_AND_TRAINER_SCALE =
  /^Your opponent reveals their hand   This attack does (  +) damage for each ([^.]+) you find there  $/;
/** The two printed nouns, mapped to the `CardFilter` members that already spell
    them. **ZERO new `CardFilter` members** — D440's test applied rather than copied,
    and it matters for the same two consumers: `retrieveNoun`'s exhaustive switch
    (interpreter.ts) and `BENCHABLE_RETRIEVAL_KINDS` (effects.ts), where D222's
    closed-world hazard means an omission from the `Set` compiles silently. D439
    refused its largest countable on exactly that cost.

    A CLOSED MAP and not a capture, `DISCARD_PILE_NOUNS`' argument one zone over: the
    tempting `^(.+) card$` → `byName` would spell any printed proper name without this
    file learning one, and would also claim nouns that match nothing in the catalog —
    a filter counting 0 on every board, scoring a card's printed base forever while
    `BUILT.attack` stepped for it (D190b/D199 at the instrument layer). **What does
    the refusing is the map, not the regex.**

    Read through `literalClauseRow` (D137) rather than a bare `.get` — neither key
    spells an apostrophe today (checked: `Trainer card` and `card` are both ASCII),
    so this is insurance rather than a live population, and it is the same call
    `DISCARD_PILE_NOUNS` makes for a key that does. */
const OPPONENT_HAND_NOUNS: ReadonlyMap<string, CardFilter> = new Map<string, CardFilter>([
                                                                                    
                                                                                    
                                              
  ["Trainer card", { kind: "trainerCard" }],
                                                                             
                                                                                   
                                                                             
                                                         
  ["card", { kind: "anyCard" }],
]);
                                                                         
                                                                                
                                                                               

                                                                                    
                                                                                
                            
function opponentHandFilter(noun: string): CardFilter | null {
  return literalClauseRow(OPPONENT_HAND_NOUNS, noun) ?? null;
}
                                                                                  
                                                                                
                                                                                   
                                                                                    
                                                                                 
                                                                                   
                                                                   
  
                                                               
                                                                                 
                                                                                 
                                                                             
                                                                                  
                                                         
  
                                                                             
                                          
                                                                               
                                                                             
                                                                              
                                                 
                                                                                  
                                                                             
                                                                              
                                                                                 
  
                                                                               
                                                                                
                                                                                  
                                                                               
                                                                                
                                                                               
                                                                              
                                                   
  
                                                                               
                                                                                   
                                                                                 
                                                                                   
                                                                               
                                                                                 
                                                                              
                                                                                  
                                                                                
                                                                               
                                                                 
  
                                                                          
                                                                                 
                                                                           
                                                                               
                                                                       
                                                                    
                                                                             
                                                                                  
                                            
                                                                                   
                                                                                   
                                                                                  
                                                                               
                                                                                
                                         
  
                                                                             
                                                                                 
                                                                            
                                                                                  
                                                                                  
                                                                            
                                          
  
                                                                              
                                                                           
                                                                              
                                                                               
                                                                                 
                                                                                
                                                                           
                                                                              
                                                                                 
                                                                      
